This page documents a [[id:F44766FA-1E9C-416F-849A-E131101B2ECA][user journey]]: {{description}}

A user journey describes what one person is trying to do, before anything is
built. It is a design document that outlives any sprint, so it names the
screens, the entity fields each screen shows, and the operations and messages
each step needs.

* Goal

(One or two sentences, in the person's own words: what are they trying to
achieve, and what tells them they have finished?)

* Actor and trigger

(Who runs this journey. What brings them here. Where it starts and where it
ends. Say which actor it is: the member acting on their own record, or a tenant
administrator acting inside their tenant.)

* Steps

(The ordered steps. For each step, say what the person does and what the system
does in reply. A step that needs the server to finish something later is called
out, because it decides whether the journey carries state.)

* Screens and wireframes

(Sketch each screen with PlantUML, export it to PNG beside this file, then embed
it here. See
[[id:EADD51F7-9F3E-4B03-8750-D7ABC995FE46][How do I add a PlantUML diagram?]].
A journey is one screen composed around a goal, not one screen per entity, so a
wireframe shows the panels together rather than each field set alone.)

